# Keep the build context to SOURCE ONLY.
#
# The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` for BOTH trees (root and app/) inside a
# linux/amd64 build stage, and better-sqlite3 + Vite's bundler ship native
# binaries. A host-built node_modules/ is macOS/arm64, so letting it into the
# context would have `COPY app ./app` overwrite the correctly-built Linux
# modules with unusable ones — the image would build and then fail at runtime.
node_modules
app/node_modules
web/node_modules

# Build outputs are produced inside the image, never copied from the host.
dist
app/dist

# A local dev database must never end up baked into the image: it would ship
# one developer's tenants and encrypted secrets to every deploy, and then be
# shadowed by the Fly volume mounted at /data anyway.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

.git
.github
.superpowers
docs
reference
test
gates
fixture
*.tgz
.env
.env.*
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
